 "source": "avatars_sheet.png",
 "note": "R4. One face per avatar id, in balance order. Each bust is painted inside its own gold frame with a small gold bracket in each corner. The face is cut square inside it -- 23 in from the frame's outer left edge and 8 down, clear of the frame bar and of the top brackets -- at the painting's own 236 px, which is the battle's portrait; so the crown on the king and the crest on the knight's helmet stay whole. Every screen puts its own frame round it (the card's baked frame, a rarity ring, a battle ring). A 96 px cut of the same square serves rows drawn at 68-76, which a 236 texture would alias at without mipmaps. A round cut of the same square, 160 across, is for the round windows the rankings paint (the podium's three rings, 111 to 132 across, and the rows' 66): the portrait's own disc, drawn down.",
